\DOC X86_VSTEPS_TAC

\TYPE {X86_VSTEPS_TAC : thm * (thm option array) -> int list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Symbolically executes a specified consecutive block of x86 instructions in an
{eventually}-style goal, advancing the goal's current state variable and
recording the resulting state facts as assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
{X86_VSTEPS_TAC th snums} takes {th : thm * (thm option array)}, the execution
record for the program under verification (a code-length theorem paired with
per-instruction decoding theorems), used to decode and step the instructions,
and {snums : int list}, the list of step numbers to execute, which fixes the
names of the intermediate state variables introduced (one per step). For each
step number in {snums}, in order, a fresh state variable is introduced together
with assumptions describing that state: register, flag, vector-register, memory
and event-trace reads, the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation from the initial
state to the new state, and a {bytes_loaded} fact for the final new state. The
{bytes_loaded} assumption and the {MAYCHANGE} assumption for the previous
current state are dropped, being superseded by their counterparts for the new
state; all other prior assumptions are kept unchanged. The conclusion keeps its
shape, with the {eventually} postcondition untouched and only the trailing
state argument replaced by the final new state variable {u}, with {B} the newly
added state facts:
{
       A ?- eventually ... t
    ======================== X86_VSTEPS_TAC th snums
       A, B ?- eventually ... u
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this single kind of outcome occurs, on goals of
this {eventually} form with a current-state argument.

\ENDDOC
